  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "bugfix",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Llama already requested FP32 down-projection output, but its gate and up projections still defaulted to FP16. That left two earlier points where large values could overflow: when the projection results were stored and when the half-precision activation kernel multiplied them. Widening the down result cannot recover information lost at either point.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_e907cc92edd04f99a4e4c314ec8f82ca",
          "call_5b327eb2c1214630bf4c89e508ed6d64",
          "call_23714e7b39634627b82817999a30fe42",
          "call_9256c7f2aaee4211908f1e80574479e5",
          "call_33b6a619704a4d7b9ead0f34eb946152"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The one-line change sets interm_dtype=torch.float on every GatedMLP built by LlamaModel. That setting controls both gate and up result buffers. Their FP32 outputs select the existing float SiLU-multiply kernel, which computes the product in float, converts it to half, and clamps the converted result. The down projection still consumes half and produces float. The earlier change that gave GatedMLP a separate half activation destination is a precondition for this path: writing into the float up buffer would fail the wrapper's output-dtype check.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_58019fda08954b92a5adaafcffd33f5e",
          "call_5b327eb2c1214630bf4c89e508ed6d64",
          "call_33b6a619704a4d7b9ead0f34eb946152"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "The change also reaches MiMoModel, MistralModel and Qwen2Model: each registered subclass calls LlamaModel.__init__ without replacing its MLP construction. It does not change GatedMLP's default or other models' independent constructor calls.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_58019fda08954b92a5adaafcffd33f5e",
          "call_23f9af2cd8024772a99fdb09f7259900",
          "call_ec31d1d50bb8442099330473284e7ff2",
          "call_2aec31f72d384458956c8e13c9b361a8",
          "call_84cb45660be24a7eb65c020fdcdcc272",
          "call_4823308473114af1a83c859792483f55",
          "call_5b327eb2c1214630bf4c89e508ed6d64",
          "call_98da4dadbdaa440c950fd7b088b1ed8e"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The tradeoff is wider gate and up temporaries and a different arithmetic path, not larger checkpoint weights or an FP32 down-projection input. Saturation bounds the half result at the activation boundary; it does not preserve products beyond half range exactly or establish that every source of nonfinite values is removed.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_58019fda08954b92a5adaafcffd33f5e",
          "call_5b327eb2c1214630bf4c89e508ed6d64",
          "call_6922c997f0f14fecac0066b4cc7ebddd",
          "call_33b6a619704a4d7b9ead0f34eb946152"
        ]
      }
    ],
